  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 90,
  "sortOrder": 19090,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Lord, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou art God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are as a sleep: in the morning they are like grass which groweth up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret sins in the light of thy countenance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale that is told.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "The days of our years are threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength they be fourscore years, yet is their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, so is thy wrath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Return, O LORD, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Make us glad according to the days wherein thou hast afflicted us, and the years wherein we have seen evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:90:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 90:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:90:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
